The '''1998 United States Senate election in Arkansas''' was held on November 3, 1998. [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democratic]] incumbent [[Dale Bumpers]] retired instead of seeking reelection to a fifth term. Democratic former [[United States House of Representatives|U.S. Representative]] [[Blanche Lincoln]] won the open seat against [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]] state senator [[Fay Boozman]]. At 38, Lincoln was the youngest woman ever elected to the United States Senate and the first woman elected to the Senate from Arkansas since [[Hattie Carraway]] in [[1938 United States Senate election in Arkansas|1938]]. 

In [[2010 United States Senate election in Arkansas|2010]], Lincoln lost re-election to a third term by Fay Boozman's brother, [[John Boozman]].

